('LookupBase')`\n3. `get_info('AnsiblePlugin.set_options')`\n4. `get_info('AnsiblePlugin.get_option')`\n\nThen based on results, maybe more queries.\n\nNow let me draft the tests:\n\n```python\nimport io\n\nimport pytest\n\nfrom ansible.errors import AnsibleError\nfrom ansible.module_utils.six.moves.urllib.error import HTTPError, URLError\nfrom ansible.module_utils.urls import ConnectionError, SSLValidationError\nfrom ansible.plugins.lookup import url as url_lookup_module\nfrom ansible.plugins.lookup.url import LookupModule\n\n\nclass FakeResponse(object):\n    def __init__(self, data=b''):\n        self._data = data\n\n    def read(self):\n        return self._data\n\n\n@pytest.fixture\ndef lookup_module(monkeypatch):\n    lm = LookupModule()\n    options = {\n        'validate_certs': True,\n        'use_proxy': True,\n        'username': None,\n        'password': None,\n        'headers': {},\n        'force': False,\n        'timeout': 10,\n        'http_agent': 'ansible-httpget',\n        'force_basic_auth': False,\n        'follow_redirects': 'urllib2',\n        'use_gssapi': False,\n        'unix_socket': None,\n        'ca_path': None,\n        'unredirected_headers': ['authorization', 'cookie'],\n        'split_lines': True,\n    }\n\n    def set_options(var_options=None, direct=None):\n        opts = dict(options)\n        if direct:\n            opts.update(direct)\n        lm._options = opts\n\n    monkeypatch.setattr(lm, 'set_options', set_options)\n    return lm\n```\n\nWait, but `direct` is `kwargs` passed to run(). So if the test calls `lm.run(['http://x'], split_lines=False)`, then `direct = {'split_lines': False}` and our fake set_options merges it. That way the real option flow is simulated and `split_lines=False` branch is exercised via kwargs. \n\nBut careful: `run(self, terms, variables=None, **kwargs)` \u2014 kwargs would include `split_lines=False`. Then `set_options(var_options=variables, direct=kwargs)`. Our fake merges direct into options