        if option in self._options:\n            return self._options[option]\n        else:\n            raise AnsibleError('Unknown argument to plugin (%s): %s' % (self._load_name, option))\n```\n\nHmm, I'm not sure about the exact else branch. There was a change where get_option could fall back to config defaults... Let me check via get_info.\n\nActually, I remember in ansible-core 2.15:\n\n```python\n    def get_option(self, option, plugin_vars=None, hostvars=None):\n        if option in self._options:\n            return self._options[option]\n        else:\n            raise AnsibleError('Unknown argument to plugin (%s): %s' % (self._load_name, option))\n```\n\nHmm, but there's also `_set_option`... Whatever \u2014 get_info will tell us.\n\nLet me also double check the plugin source itself via get_info('LookupModule') to confirm the exact code and imports (e.g., whether it's `from ansible.module_utils.urls import open_url, ConnectionError, SSLValidationError`).\n\nAlright, let me make the get_info calls now.\n\nRound 1 (independent):\n- get_info('LookupModule')\n- get_info('AnsiblePlugin.set_options')\n- get_info('AnsiblePlugin.get_option')\n- get_info('LookupBase')\n\nThen round 2 if needed:\n- get_info('SSLValidationError')\n- get_info('ConnectionError')\n- get_info('HTTPError')\n\nLet me do round 1.\n\nAfter that, I'll write the final test script.\n\nDraft final test script:\n\n```python\n# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-\n\"\"\"Tests for ansible/plugins/lookup/url.py covering lines 190-224.\"\"\"\n\nimport io\n\nimport pytest\n\nfrom ansible.errors import AnsibleError\nfrom ansible.module_utils._text import to_native, to_text\nfrom ansible.module_utils.six.moves.urllib.error import HTTPError, URLError\nfrom ansible.module_utils.urls import ConnectionError, SSLValidationError\nfrom ansible.plugins.lookup import url as url_lookup\nfrom ansible.plugins.lookup.url import LookupModule\n\n\nclass FakeResponse(object):\n    \"\"\"Minimal stand-in for the file-like object returned by open_url.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, data=b''):\n        self._data = data\n        self.read_calls = 0\n\n    def read(self):\n        self.read_calls += 1\n        return self._data\n\n\nDEFAULT_OPTIONS = {\n    'validate_certs': True,\n    'use_proxy': True,\n    'username': None,\n    'password': None,\n    'headers': {},\n    'force': False,\n    'timeout': 10,\n    'http_agent': 'ansible-httpget',\n    'force_basic_auth': False,\n    'follow_redirects': 'urllib2',\n    'use_gssapi': False,\n    'unix_socket': None,\n    'ca_path': None,\n    'unredirected_headers': ['authorization', 'cookie'],\n    'split_lines': True,\n}\n\n\n@pytest.fixture\ndef lookup(monkeypatch):\n    \"\"\"LookupModule with a lightweight set_options that mimics option handling.\"\"\"\n    lm = LookupModule()\n\n    def fake_set_options(var_options=None, direct=None):\n        options = dict(DEFAULT_OPTIONS)\n        if direct:\n            options.update(direct)\n        lm._options = options\n\n    monkeypatch.setattr(lm, 'set_options', fake_set_options)\n    return lm\n\n\n@pytest.fixture\ndef open_url_mock(monkeypatch):\n    \"\"\"Patch open_url in the plugin module; records calls, returns canned responses.\"\"\"\n    calls = []\n    responses = []\n\n    def fake_open_url(term, **kwargs):\n        calls.append((term, kwargs))\n        if responses:\n            result = responses.pop(0)\n            if isinstance(result, Exception):\n                raise result\n            return result\n        return FakeResponse(b'')\n\n    monkeypatch.setattr(url_lookup, 'open_url', fake_open_url)\n    fake_open_url.calls = calls\n    fake_open_url.responses = responses\n    return fake_open_url\n```\n\nHmm, wait: `monkeypatch.setattr(lm, 'set_options', fake_set_options)` \u2014 setting an attribute on an instance. monkeypatch.setattr works with (target, name, value). For instance attributes, it should work: `monkeypatch.setattr(lm, 'set_options', fake_set_options)` \u2014 it does getattr for undo, setattr new. Fine.\n\nBut careful: since `fake_set_options` is a plain function assigned as instance attribute, calling `lm.set_options(var_options=variables, direct=kwargs)` calls it without self. Our signature matches (var_options=None, direct=None). Good.\n\nNow tests:\n\n```python\ndef test_run_single_term_split_lines(lookup, open_url_mock):\n    response = FakeResponse(b'line1\\nline2\\nline3\\n')\n    open_url_mock.responses.append(response)\n\n    result = lookup.run(['http://ansible.example.com/'])\n\n    assert result == ['line1', 'line2', 'line3']\n    assert len(open_url_mock.calls) == 1\n    term, kwargs = open_url_mock.calls[0]\n    assert term == 'http://ansible.example.com/'\n    # all options are forwarded to open_url\n    assert kwargs['validate_certs'] is True\n    assert kwargs['use_proxy'] is True\n    assert kwargs['username'] is None\n    assert kwargs['password'] is None\n    assert kwargs['headers'] == {}\n    assert kwargs['force'] is False\n    assert kwargs['timeout'] == 10\n    assert kwargs['http_agent'] == 'ansible-httpget'\n    assert kwargs['force_basic_auth'] is False\n    assert kwargs['follow_redirects'] == 'urllib2'\n    assert kwargs['use_gssapi'] is False\n    assert kwargs['unix_socket'] is None\n    assert kwargs['ca_path'] is None\n    assert kwargs['unredirected_headers'] == ['authorization', 'cookie']\n    assert response.read_calls == 1\n```\n\nWait \u2014 `splitlines()` on `b'line1\\nline2\\nline3\\n'` gives `[b'line1', b'line2', b'line3']`. Good.\n\n```python\ndef test_run_split_lines_false(lookup, open_url_mock):\n    open_url_mock.responses.append(FakeResponse(b'one\\ntwo\\nthree'))\n\n    result = lookup.run(['http://ansible.example.com/'], split_lines=False)\n\n    assert result == ['one\\ntwo\\nthree']\n```\n\nThis covers line 223 (else branch).\n\n```python\ndef test_run_multiple_terms(lookup, open_url_mock):\n    open_url_mock.responses.append(FakeResponse(b'a\\nb'))\n    open_url_mock.responses.append(FakeResponse(b'c\\nd'))\n\n    result = lookup.run(['http://one.example.com/', 'http://two.example.com/'])\n\n    assert result == ['a', 'b', 'c', 'd']\n    assert [term for term, kwargs in open_url_mock.calls] == ['http://one.example.com/', 'http://two.example.com/']\n```\n\n```python\ndef test_run_http_error(lookup, open_url_mock):\n    open_url_mock.responses.append(HTTPError('http://ansible.example.com/', 500, 'Internal Server Error', None, io.BytesIO(b'oops')))\n\n    with pytest.raises(AnsibleError) as excinfo:\n        lookup.run(['http://ansible.example.com/'])\n\n    assert 'Received HTTP error for http://ansible.example.com/' in to_native(excinfo.value)\n```\n\nHmm, the message format: `\"Received HTTP error for %s : %s\" % (term, to_native(e))`. So the message is 'Received HTTP error for http://... : HTTP Error 500: Internal Server Error'. Assert 'Received HTTP error for' in message and term in message.\n\n```python\ndef test_run_url_error(lookup, open_url_mock):\n    open_url_mock.responses.append(URLError('connection refused'))\n\n    with pytest.raises(AnsibleError) as excinfo:\n        lookup.run(['http://ansible.example.com/'])\n\n    assert 'Failed lookup url for http://ansible.example.com/' in to_native(excinfo.value)\n```\n\n```python\ndef test_run_ssl_validation_error(lookup, open_url_mock):\n    open_url_mock.responses.append(SSLValidationError('certificate verify failed'))\n\n    with pytest.raises(AnsibleError) as excinfo:\n        lookup.run(['https://ansible.example.com/'])\n\n    assert \"Error validating the server's certificate for https://ansible.example.com/\" in to_native(excinfo.value)\n```\n\n```python\ndef test_run_connection_error(lookup, open_url_mock):\n    open_url_mock.responses.append(ConnectionError('timed out'))\n\n    with pytest.raises(AnsibleError) as excinfo:\n        lookup.run(['http://ansible.example.com/'])\n\n    assert 'Error connecting to http://ansible.example.com/' in to_native(excinfo.value)\n```\n\nAlso maybe a test that verifies HTTPError takes precedence over URLError (since HTTPError subclasses URLError) \u2014 implicitly covered.\n\nAlso a test that verifies the exception propagates and stops processing further terms? Not needed.\n\nAlso test that `variables` are passed to set_options: we could assert our fake set_options received var_options. Let's add a test:\n\n```python\ndef test_run_passes_variables_to_set_options(lookup, open_url_mock, monkeypatch):\n    captured = {}\n    original = lookup.set_options  # the monkeypatched fake\n    ...\n```\n\nHmm, this is getting complicated. Simpler: in the fixture, record calls:\n\n```python\n@pytest.fixture\ndef lookup(monkeypatch):\n    lm = LookupModule()\n    lm._set_options_calls = []\n\n    def fake_set_options(var_options=None, direct=None):\n        lm._set_options_calls.append({'var_options': var_options, 'direct': direct})\n        options = dict(DEFAULT_OPTIONS)\n        if direct:\n            options.update(direct)\n        lm._options = options\n\n    monkeypatch.setattr(lm, 'set_options', fake_set_options)\n    return lm\n```\n\nThen a test:\n\n```python\ndef test_run_forwards_variables_and_kwargs(lookup, open_url_mock):\n    lookup.run(['http://ansible.example.com/'], variables={'url_split_lines': False}, split_lines=False)\n    call = lookup._set_options_calls[0]\n    assert call['var_options'] == {'url_split_lines': False}\n    assert call['direct'] == {'split_lines': False}\n```\n\nHmm wait, `run(self, terms, variables=None, **kwargs)` \u2014 calling `lookup.run([...], variables={...}, split_lines=False)`. Then `set_options(var_options=variables, direct=kwargs)` where kwargs={'split_lines': False}. Good.\n\nHmm, but wait: does `run` accept `variables` as keyword? Yes: `def run(self, terms, variables=None, **kwargs)`. Good.\n\nNow \u2014 one concern: `display.vvvv(\"url lookup connecting to %s\" % term)`. The `display` object in the plugin module. Calling vvvv is harmless. But in some test enviro